import json
d=json.load(open('/output/report.json'))
A=json.load(open('/snapshots/team-a-s29/TEAM_REPORT.json'))['results']
B=json.load(open('/snapshots/team-b-s26/TEAM_REPORT.json'))['results']
def add(src,i,pre,conf=None,note=''):
    x=dict(src[i]); x['evidence']=pre+x['evidence']
    if note: x['value']=note+x['value']
    if conf: x['confidence']=conf
    d['results'].append(x)
pa='team-a posts p0048-p0052 [snapshots /snapshots/team-a-s24..s29, TEAM_REPORT.json of team-a-s29; scripts under each snapshot scripts/]. '
pb='team-b p0050 [snapshot /snapshots/team-b-s26; scripts s250*_q42*.py, out/q42/; team-a replication p0050-r01 /snapshots/team-a-s29 q47_*]. '
add(A,212,pa,'tentative','[RETRACTED by team-a p0051/p0048-r01: SMC sampler noise; do not quote Tc_N 24->14 K or P(Te>=50) 0.45->0.37. Superseded by the nested-sampling entries below.] ')
for i in range(213,218): add(A,i,'team-a p0049 [snapshot /snapshots/team-a-s25, scripts q40*.py, out/q40b/]. ' if i<218 else pa)
for i in range(218,221): add(A,i,pa)
for i in range(221,224): add(A,i,'team-a p0050-r01 [snapshot /snapshots/team-a-s29, scripts q47_*.py, out/q47/]. ')
for i in range(216,221): add(B,i,pb)
d['interpretation']+=("\n\n=== UPDATE 7 (team-a p0048-p0052, team-b p0050 and replies) ===\n"
"Temperature. The SMC numbers of p0042/p0044/p0046/p0048 (Tc_N 24 K with 1-0, 14 K without; P(Te>=50)=0.45/0.37) are RETRACTED by their author (p0048-r01, p0051): under convergent nested sampling Tc_S = 17+/-1 K (single-nucleus 12-28 K, >60 K disfavoured by dchi2 5-11) is robust, but Tc_N is unconstrained (12-95 K, dchi2<5 over 10-150 K; median 45 vs 22 K with/without 1-0, seed sd ~11 K), also in N-only fits, so the shared envelope is not the cause; the sign of Tc_N-Tc_S is undefined (P 0.4-0.84). The envelope P(Te>=50) is prior-dependent (0.67 at band-scale sigma 0.10, 0.24 at 0.25). Therefore no nucleus-to-nucleus temperature difference is established, and the earlier Q22 envelope-temperature statements (Te ~53 K) should be read as 'warm envelope allowed, not required'. IR pumping: strong 14 um pumping (T_IR>=150 K, W>=0.3) is disfavoured (dlnZ -4..-10) but this is model-dependent.\n"
"Opacity / isotopes. H13CN 4-3 is not detected; the limit alpha<=0.10-0.12 (HCN/H13CN>=8-10 at N; S >=7) is reproduced by both teams once only chi2-acceptable CO 3-2 wing models are kept. RADEX predicts alpha 0.016-0.035 in every branch (trapped thick HCN, subthermal H13CN), so the 4-3 limit cannot separate the cold-thick from the hot branch at N; earlier 'tau<...' bounds are equal-Tex statements only. At a common 2.2\" taper H13CO+/HCO+ is 0.023+/-0.003 (N) vs 0.018+/-0.004 (S) and H13CN/HCN 0.021+/-0.003 (N) vs 0.006+/-0.006 (S, undetected): N-S differences are <=2 sigma. X_S/X_N is NOT established: team-b gets 1.3-1.8 (<=2 sigma), team-a's replication gets median 0.98 (95% 0.45-2.55), i.e. unconstrained; the earlier Q40 contrast of ~2.5 was mostly beam/aperture mixing. The 1-0 12C lines are not thin (RADEX tau10 HCN 4.6 N, 5.7 S). The cold/dense optically thick branch at N is disfavoured (P<=0.07) only under tight (10/15%) band-scale priors, not excluded otherwise (team-a's own 13C-in-likelihood test: P(Tc_N<=30)=0.26-0.32 vs 0.40, not reproducing team-b's shifts). Net: opacity vs abundance is still not separated at N; abundance (N(HCN)/N(HCO+) 1.5-3.4 higher at N) and thick-line explanations both survive.\n"
"Clumps. At matched uv and a 8.64x6.0\" beam the HCN/HCO+ ratio at E1 and W is below that of N+S at every J (E1/(N+S) 0.72, 0.60, 0.47 at 1-0, 2-1, 3-2; W 0.70, 0.75, 0.63); the E1 deepening with J is ~2.7 sigma (qualitative), W is flat; the 'mostly 1-0' wording is not supported, and the Harada vs Michiyama 1-0 discrepancy at E1/W is uv filtering. This is outside the main question; it only shows that low ratios occur away from the AGN too. Conclusion on the primary target is unchanged: the N/S contrast (about 2) is real, carried by HCN, J-independent for ~60% (log) with at most ~40% from excitation, and the data cannot decide among an HCN abundance excess at N, a lower HCN opacity/column at S, or a temperature difference; the AGN nucleus does not show HCN enhancement, so HCN/HCO+ is not a usable AGN diagnostic in this merger.")
d['caveats'].append("p0048-p0052: Tc_N posteriors are not converged (seed scatter 11-24 K in the median, logZ scatter exceeds quoted error): use quantiles, not medians; the H13CN reweighting is post hoc and wing-model dependent; team-b's one-zone Harada-intensity fit script was not available to team-a, so the band-scale-prior dependence of the cold-branch exclusion (team-b p0050) is not independently reproduced; the 13C fits mix 2.2\" ratios with 1.7\" 12C intensities and H13CO+ uses the HCO+ LAMDA file. An independent thermometer at N (CH3CN, HC3N, CH3OH ladders, HCN/HCO+ >=5-4) or matched-taper H13CN 3-2 would settle Tc_N and opacity.")
d['recipe'].append({'order':19,'stage':'verification','description':'Synthesis update 7: read p0048-p0052 and replies; merged the new results of team-a-s29 (Q40-Q50, Q47) and team-b-s26 (Q40, Q38, Q42a-c) TEAM_REPORT.json; marked the SMC Q39 result as retracted.','software':'python json','parameters':[],'scripts':['/workspace/synth/update7.py']})
# annotate superseded temperature entries
note=' [UPDATE 7: SMC-based Tc/P(Te>=50) quoted here are retracted by team-a (p0051): Tc_S=17+/-1 K robust, Tc_N unconstrained, P(Te>=50) prior-dependent 0.24-0.67; read as warm envelope allowed, not required.]'
for i in (201,202,203,205,210):
    d['results'][i]['value']+=note
